<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">PentestBlueprint</a><span>/</span><a href="/dark-codex">The Dark Codex</a><span>/</span><span>BloodHound / RustHound</span></nav>
<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">THE DARK CODEX / ACTIVE DIRECTORY</p><h1>BloodHound / RustHound<span>.</span></h1><p class="lead">Collect and analyze directory privilege relationships. RustHound-CE collects Active Directory relationships; BloodHound CE visualizes them as a graph to support access-path analysis.</p></header>
<img class="hero-img" src="/images/dark-codex/bloodhound.png" alt="BloodHound / RustHound Dark Codex cover" loading="eager" width="768" height="256" />
<div class="note"><strong>Scope:</strong> These examples are intended for systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess. Replace placeholders with lab values. CLI options can change between releases; check each tool's <code>--help</code> output.</div>
<div class="body-grid"><article>
<section class="section" id="commands"><p class="eyebrow">01 / FIELD COMMANDS</p><h2>Commands you'll actually use</h2><div class="examples"><div class="example"><h3>Collector help</h3><p>Check installed RustHound-CE syntax and collection options.</p><pre><code>rusthound-ce --help</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Authenticated collection</h3><p>Collect domain data with an authorized account; options may differ by release.</p><pre><code>rusthound-ce -d &lt;domain&gt; -u &lt;user&gt; -p &lt;password&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>BloodHound Python help</h3><p>Check whether the Python collector is installed and its supported flags.</p><pre><code>bloodhound-python --help</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Python collector example</h3><p>Collect common AD data for supported BloodHound workflows; check CE compatibility.</p><pre><code>bloodhound-python -d &lt;domain&gt; -u &lt;user&gt; -p &lt;password&gt; -ns &lt;dc-ip&gt; -c All</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Start BloodHound CE</h3><p>Start a locally installed BloodHound CE deployment if bloodhound-cli is configured.</p><pre><code>bloodhound-cli up</code></pre></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="concepts"><p class="eyebrow">02 / REMEMBER THIS</p><h2>Key concepts and flags</h2><div class="terms"><div class="term"><strong>Collection</strong><p>Collectors query directory relationships and produce importable data.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Graph edges</strong><p>An edge represents a relationship or possible permission, not automatic exploitation.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Version match</strong><p>Use collectors compatible with your BloodHound edition.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="workflow"><p class="eyebrow">03 / FIELD NOTES</p><h2>Practical reminders</h2><ul><li>After importing data, investigate the reason for each privilege edge.</li><li>Collection may be incomplete when LDAP, RPC, or other services are filtered.</li></ul></section>
<section class="section sources" id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">04 / SOURCES & CREDITS</p><h2>Documentation and attribution</h2><p>This is an independently written PentestBlueprint quick reference informed by the official project documentation below. Tool names and trademarks belong to their respective projects; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.</p><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/SpecterOps/bloodhound-docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SpecterOps BloodHound documentation ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/g0h4n/RustHound-CE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RustHound-CE project ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://docs.rs/crate/rusthound-ce/latest" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RustHound-CE package documentation ↗</a></li></ul></section>
</article><aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong><a href="#commands">Common commands</a><a href="#concepts">Key concepts</a><a href="#workflow">Field reminders</a><a href="#sources">Sources & credits</a></aside></div>
